body:
is it true that only one nvm device is supported with FDP enabled? Please comment if multiple NVM is supported in newer releases. I am using stable release v20240621 right now.

In Device.cpp, within the createDirectIoFileDevice() function:

```
if (isFDPEnabled) {
  try {
    if (filePaths.size() > 1) {
      throw std::invalid_argument(folly::sformat(
          "{} input files; but FDP mode does not support RAID files yet",
          filePaths.size()));
    }
```
This logic explicitly disallows multiple input files (i.e., multiple NVMe devices) when deviceEnableFDP: true.
It throws an exception if more than one file/device is passed,


**also**
```
fdpNvmeVec.push_back(std::move(fdpNvme));
...
static constexpr uint16_t kDefaultFdpIdx = 0u;
return fdpNvmeVec_[kDefaultFdpIdx]->allocateFdpHandle();
```
So even though a vector is used (fdpNvmeVec_), only index 0 is ever accessed. This confirms only one FDP-enabled NVMe device is allowed and utilized.

### Summary
Added a new slabrebalance strategy: `MarginalHitsStrategyNew`, which builds upon the existing `MarginalHitsStrategy`. The goal is to mitigate slab thrashing issues by adding tuning mechanisms.


---

### Different Strategy Configurations for Testing

The following configurations are supported and can be tested for performance comparison:

#### Option 1: Hits-Per-Slab

```cpp
#include "cachelib/allocator/HitsPerSlabStrategy.h"

auto rbConfig = HitsPerSlabStrategy::Config{};
config.enablePoolRebalancing(
  std::make_shared<HitsPerSlabStrategy>(rbConfig),
  std::chrono::seconds(1));
```

---

#### Option 2: Marginal-Hits (Original) + Warm Tail + Cold Tail

```cpp
#include "cachelib/allocator/MarginalHitsStrategy.h"

config.enableTailHitsTracking(); 
config.countColdTailHitsOnly = false;
auto rbConfig = MarginalHitsStrategy::Config{};
config.enablePoolRebalancing(
  std::make_shared<MarginalHitsStrategy>(rbConfig),
  std::chrono::seconds(1));
```

---

#### Option 3: Marginal-Hits (Original) + Cold Tail Only

```cpp
#include "cachelib/allocator/MarginalHitsStrategy.h"

config.enableTailHitsTracking(); 
config.countColdTailHitsOnly = true;
auto rbConfig = MarginalHitsStrategy::Config{};
config.enablePoolRebalancing(
  std::make_shared<MarginalHitsStrategy>(rbConfig),
  std::chrono::seconds(1));
```

---

#### Option 4: Marginal-Hits-New (Tuned) + Warm Tail + Cold Tail

```cpp
#include "cachelib/allocator/MarginalHitsStrategyNew.h"

config.enableTailHitsTracking(); 
config.countColdTailHitsOnly = false;
auto rbConfig = MarginalHitsStrategyNew::Config{};
config.enablePoolRebalancing(
  std::make_shared<MarginalHitsStrategyNew>(rbConfig),
  std::chrono::seconds(1));
```

---

#### Option 5: Marginal-Hits-New (Tuned) + Cold Tail Only

```cpp
#include "cachelib/allocator/MarginalHitsStrategyNew.h"

config.enableTailHitsTracking(); 
config.countColdTailHitsOnly = true;
auto rbConfig = MarginalHitsStrategyNew::Config{};
config.enablePoolRebalancing(
  std::make_shared<MarginalHitsStrategyNew>(rbConfig),
  std::chrono::seconds(1));
```

---

#### Option 6: LRU-Tail-Age

```cpp
#include "cachelib/allocator/LruTailAgeStrategy.h"

auto rbConfig = LruTailAgeStrategy::Config{};
config.enablePoolRebalancing(
  std::make_shared<LruTailAgeStrategy>(rbConfig),
  std::chrono::seconds(1));
```

